{"availability":"available","full":"leofyada/splitfile-app","name":"splitfile-app","description":"Streamlit app to split one file into multiple files based on a column.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":1,"created":"2021-04-15T04:06:09Z","updated":"2026-08-17T20:32:44Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://leofyada-de-heroku-programa-de-lsy865.streamlit.app/","topics":["python","streamlit"],"demo":"https://leofyada-de-heroku-programa-de-lsy865.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:59.998Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:59.998Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:59.998Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:38.243Z","stars":0,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-16T02:45:59.998Z","stars":0,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Streamlit is an open-source Python library that enables you to create web applications.","The São Paulo State Department of Education (SEDUC-SP) has 91 regional administrative units (DEs), which are responsible for managing all the state public schools. One of the challenges faced by SEDUC-SP is that the IT team usually creates files with data per DE in a single file. In order to send the data separatly to each DE, it was necessary to split into 91 files. In this context, I created this application to automatize this task."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/leofyada/splitfile-app/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"da2a054d338017f9fa932d4b9621c3c1de222e8e747424108e653573f5e14c4f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:38.406Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:38.406Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Streamlit is an open-source Python library that enables you to create web applications.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/leofyada/splitfile-app/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"da2a054d338017f9fa932d4b9621c3c1de222e8e747424108e653573f5e14c4f","sourceUrl":"https://git